      "evidence": "scripts/check_ci_python.py:262-263: `version = str(options.get(\"python-version\", \"\"))` followed by `VERSION.fullmatch(version)`. design.md says the value must be \"a string or number matching ^3\\.\\d+$\". Numbers are not tested; the tests only use quoted strings. The current ci.yml quotes \"3.11\", so there is no live impact today. A fix would be to refuse non-string values or read the raw text.",
      "id": "unquoted-yaml-version-misread",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "An unquoted YAML `python-version: 3.10` is parsed as the float 3.1. `str()` turns it into \"3.1\", which passes the `^3\\.\\d+$` check, so the script would look for `python3.1` or compare against the wrong minor version. The design says a number is accepted, but this case is not handled or tested."
    }
